# XPact API requests: open in VS Code (REST Client), Visual Studio or Rider and click "Send".
# The same requests are in xpact-api.postman_collection.json for Postman.
@base = http://localhost:5080

### Health
GET {{base}}/api/health

### Builds and limits
GET {{base}}/api/info

### Validate pasted XML (JSON body) – accepted
POST {{base}}/api/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "xml": "<catalog><item id=\"1\">Book</item></catalog>" }

### Mismatched tag – rejected with code 7 and its line/column
POST {{base}}/api/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "xml": "<root>\n  <child>\n</root>", "build": "assertions" }

### Feed the document 1 byte at a time
POST {{base}}/api/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{ "xml": "<root><a>1</a></root>", "chunkSize": 1 }

### Raw XML body (as curl --data-binary @file.xml)
POST {{base}}/api/validate?build=production
Content-Type: application/xml

<root><a b="1"/></root>

### Upload a file (multipart form)
POST {{base}}/api/validate
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=xpact

--xpact
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="build"

production
--xpact
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.xml"
Content-Type: application/xml

<note><to>Tove</to><from>Jani</from></note>
--xpact--

### W3C conformance numbers
GET {{base}}/api/results/conformance

### Benchmark numbers
GET {{base}}/api/results/benchmarks
